{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": [
        "U9",
        "J6",
        "J10",
        "U4"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "U9.7",
        "J6.2",
        "J10.2",
        "U4.13"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "Net-(J10-Pin_2)",
        "/Microcontroller/NET0007"
      ],
      "observed": "In the netlist, the TPS1H200 high-side switch output pin 7 is connected to J10 pin 2 (Net-(J10-Pin_2)), while J6 pin 2 is connected to the MCU GPIO1 / heater-control net (/Microcontroller/NET0007) together with U9 IN/DIAG_EN and the status LED D3.",
      "expected": "The specification states that the heater switch OUT pin should feed the intended heater connector J6 pin 2, not the MCU control net.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "OUT (pin 7) feeds the heater connector J6 pin 2"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U9\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"OUT\") (pintype \"output\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J10\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J6\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If a heater is connected to the connector designated J6 in the intended design, it will see the 3.3 V GPIO1 control signal instead of the switched 12 V output from the high-side switch. The heater would not operate as intended and the ESP32 GPIO could be overstressed. The actual switched 12 V output is instead present on J10.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist otherwise matches the specified power, SPI, thermocouple, fan, and heater-switch topology, but the heater connector assignment appears anomalous: the high-side switch output is routed to J10 while J6 is tied to the MCU heater-control net, contrary to the specification."
}

